WEBVTT

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:13.430
Good.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.930
G-Good morning, Shion!

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:20.680
Good morning, Hana.

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:23.060
You're early today, huh?

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.690
I totally forgot that I'm on duty today!

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:29.820
Then wanna at least have
some milk before you go?

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:31.440
Y-Yeah!

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:36.700
See you later!

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.200
Yep! See you later!

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:53.970
Did I make it in time?

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:02.350
Ichinose...

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:07.900
Good morning.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:11.400
U-Um, uh...

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:13.990
Oh, um...

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:49.040
U-Um...

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:51.540
T-Takahashi?

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:53.800
Yeah, Nanae Takahashi.

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:56.380
Um, uh...

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:59.550
I'm sorry for being late to cleaning duty!

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:03.050
Don't worry about it. I'm always early.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:06.310
I finished our morning duties already.

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:08.690
O-Oh. Sorry.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:10.940
But thank you.

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:12.650
Not at all.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:16.400
For after school, we just have
the log and taking out the trash.

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:17.440
Which one do you want?

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:19.030
Wh-Which one?

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:20.990
Wh-Whichever one is fine!

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:23.070
I-I'll let you decide!

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:25.540
You can choose the one you like.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:29.790
Th-Then, I'll take the log out in the trash!

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:36.500
Banana chocolate mint Hawaiian!

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:40.630
HANA'S FRIENDS

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:41.470
If you get it in the morning,
all the selections are available!

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:45.430
Yeah, if you go for it in the afternoon,
sometimes only vanilla is left.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:47.600
Even though vanilla is good...

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:50.560
I always choose a more exotic flavor!

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:51.690
I know what you mean!

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:54.940
Morning ice cream is unusual
for you, Hana!

00:03:56.230 --> 00:04:00.030
Yeah. I overslept today
and didn't have time for breakfast.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:02.490
I forgot my lunch at home, too.

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:05.580
It's a shame because Shion made it for me.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:06.330
Oh dear.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:09.870
And while on duty, I was so nervous
that I said something weird,

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:12.210
which really confused Takahashi!

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:15.670
So it was the Hana-Nana combo today?

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.340
That's a charming duo!

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:23.010
I don't think Nanae is the type
to make someone nervous though.

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:26.970
But it was the first time
I talked to Takahashi.

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:28.350
Huh?

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:29.470
What?

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:32.440
I mean, the first semester is almost over.

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:36.520
I haven't talked to more than half
the students in our class.

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:37.440
What?

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:40.780
This is how it was for me
in middle school, too.

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:42.030
Unless there's an opportunity,

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:44.990
the first year will go by
without talking to most of the students.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:51.160
It's not necessary for an opportunity
as a reason to talk to someone.

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:52.540
I know, right?

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:56.170
If you're sitting close to someone,
you just start talking to them.

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:59.090
Th-That's difficult for me.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:03.090
That being said,
you talk normally to us, Hana.

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:07.350
That's right. You're not nervous
when you talk to us, right?

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:09.350
No, but...

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:11.980
That's true, but...

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:15.690
Kamu should be here by now!

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:18.730
Yeah. I just hope she's not lonely
in there without us.

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:20.110
Let's hurry!

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:22.240
<i>Come to think of it, maybe Kamuri...</i>

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:25.570
<i>would understand how I feel!</i>

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:27.740
Kamuri!

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:29.830
We have snacks! Come here!

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:31.120
Snacks...

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:33.500
And I brought cookies.

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:35.210
- Want some?
- Yep, yep.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:39.840
What kind do you want?
Chocolate or strawberry?

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:41.380
B-Both.

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:43.880
Can we take a picture of you eating?

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:47.930
- No, huh?
- Eiko...

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:50.100
- She's so cute!
- Eiko...

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:51.140
Eiko...

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:54.430
Eiko!

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:56.100
Morning, Kamu.

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:58.860
Sorry I wasn't here for you.

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:04.780
<i>She's loved without
having to make a move! It's...</i>

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:06.860
<i>a fawning framework!</i>

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:08.660
<i>Gulp!</i>

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:13.120
Ms. Hannen!

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:14.910
This is perfect timing!

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:17.250
Well, well, the landlady!

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:20.630
Listen, have you had lunch yet?

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:24.840
I had my lunch ready to go,
but didn't have a drink,

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:27.180
so I'm just coming back from buying tea

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:28.800
at the convenience store!

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:33.060
Actually, Hana forgot
to take her lunch to school,

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:36.560
so would you like to have it?

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:38.060
What?

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:39.940
Hana's lunch?

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:41.270
Are you sure?

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:43.440
I don't know if you'll like it or not.

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:49.950
I've got it! Why don't we trade,
so you can then have my lunch?

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:53.450
<i>I guess.</i>

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:54.580
<i>Once in a while.</i>

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:55.580
UME

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:58.580
Sure, why don't we trade?

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:02.960
Wow, I haven't had a homemade lunch
since high school!

00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:09.220
I'll bring mine over, so wait there!

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:11.850
<i>Good!</i>

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:19.350
Um, this is... A-Are you sure?

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:20.730
Go ahead, go ahead!

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:23.440
This looks delicious!

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:25.650
Thank you, landlady!

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:29.320
Oh no, it's not...

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:30.860
I feel kind of bad.

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:41.620
So let's have our classmates
introduce themselves to Hana!

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:43.590
Huh? Um, but...

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:45.710
And so...

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:47.550
I'm Maho Ogano!

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:49.220
I'm Amane Ohtani!

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:52.640
I-I'm Hana Ichinose!

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:55.010
You're like a comedy trio.

00:07:55.010 --> 00:07:57.720
S-Sorry! I suddenly got nervous!

00:07:58.180 --> 00:08:01.100
Weren't you in the rookie tournament
for the track and field team?

00:08:01.350 --> 00:08:02.560
How'd it go, Maho?

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:05.360
Oh, it was a disaster.

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:08.190
H-How did it go for you, Ohtani?

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:10.900
I'm the team manager.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:12.610
I'm terrible at sports myself.

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:13.620
Really?

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:19.540
When we run in P.E.,
I'm always next to you, Ichinose.

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:21.040
You never noticed?

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:22.960
P.E. is...

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:26.210
I have to focus on myself to survive.

00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:30.720
I'm Hina Sasaki!

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:33.510
I'm Ao Masuda. I'm on the volleyball team.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:35.640
Oh, I'm Yuuri Endou.

00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:37.430
I'm also on the volleyball team.

00:08:37.430 --> 00:08:39.020
N-Nice to meet you.

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:40.770
Nice to meet you.

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:43.190
Why don't you come
check us out next time?

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:45.940
We're always on the lookout
for new members.

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:48.900
I-I think ball games
are a little hard for me.

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:52.280
So if running and ball games
are ruled out,

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:53.860
how about swimming?

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:56.570
I-I-I-I have trouble with that, too!

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:01.250
I'm Kei Iwasaki!

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:02.660
I'm Sachi Tsubakimori.

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:04.670
H-Hello.

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:08.340
So you're trying to conquer
your shyness, huh? I'll help you!

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:11.170
Th-Thank you.

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:14.380
Tsubaki here is our class's
student council rep.

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:16.390
You can count on Icchi, too.

00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:17.760
I-Icchi?

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:19.720
S-Sure. Nice to meet you.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:23.180
Yes, it's nice to meet you, too.

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:27.940
S-Sorry to bother you when you're eating.

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:29.190
That's okay.

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:30.780
Salmon again?

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:32.070
You really like that, huh?

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:34.070
Yeah, I do.

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:36.070
Well, it is one of the standards.

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:39.780
Yeah, that's why I like it.

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:43.290
Sachi, you're really close...

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.960
Tsubaki, you like salmon that much?

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:56.300
Salmon has an abundance
of eicosapentaenoic acid.

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:57.260
Eiko?

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:59.970
Eicosapentaenoic acid.

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:06.560
Well, you talked normally enough.

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:08.100
D-Did I?

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:12.360
Oh, but that was with your help,
Eiko and Tama.

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:16.360
Nah, we didn't really do
anything big to help.

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:17.860
Come to think of it,

00:10:18.110 --> 00:10:20.280
Kamu is also the type who takes time.

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:23.450
But I'm used to Hana and Tama now.

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:25.710
Then I can do this?

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:31.170
Kamuri is hanging in there!

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:33.420
You're cute when you're trying
to hold back, Kamu!

00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:38.430
Let's see! How much food
are you storing in those cheeks?

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:49.400
TODAY'S SUMMARY

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:49.400
"Today I'm glad I was able to talk
to several of my classmates."

00:10:50.110 --> 00:10:51.900
- What is this?
- U-Um...

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:55.900
They introduced me
to some of our classmates.

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:57.110
Introduced?

00:10:57.360 --> 00:11:00.820
I'd never talked
to most of them before, so...

00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:02.410
Ah, I see.

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:03.790
HOMEROOM TEACHER

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:07.000
For me, if there's someone
I don't need to talk to,

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:09.420
I wouldn't go out of my way
to talk to them.

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:13.420
There's no need to force yourself.

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:15.460
You're you, Ichinose.

00:11:16.090 --> 00:11:17.510
Do it at your own pace.

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:19.260
Okay.

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:27.480
<i>My own pace...</i>

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:30.020
Good job!

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:33.190
I finished taking out the garbage.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:35.820
T-Takahashi...

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:37.360
Good job!

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:39.820
<i>I-I've got an idea!</i>

00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:43.870
<i>This time I'll talk to Takahashi
a-about something!</i>

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:50.250
Um, uh, um, uh, um...

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:53.210
Well, I'm going to my club.

00:11:55.130 --> 00:11:56.340
See you tomorrow!

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:02.050
Yeah. See you then.

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:10.640
<i>Good morning.</i>

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:16.110
Yeah.

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:20.400
Tomorrow I'll be the one
who says "good morning" first.

00:12:25.990 --> 00:12:28.580
In the beach house of a nudist beach,

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:31.330
I wonder if they make yakisoba
in the nude!

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:34.170
That'd be painful with spattering hot oil!

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:36.290
I wanna eat yakisoba.

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:39.630
I-I would think
they'd at least wear an apron.

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:43.970
Nude wearing an apron?
You're a freak, too, Hana!

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:48.060
Still, I'd like to go
to the beach this summer!

00:12:48.310 --> 00:12:49.680
Not a nude beach!

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:51.390
One where you wear a swimsuit.

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:54.440
I want a new swimsuit.

00:12:54.770 --> 00:12:57.650
My old one from middle school
doesn't fit me anymore.

00:12:57.980 --> 00:12:59.400
Wanna go shopping with me later?

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:00.650
Sure!

00:13:01.190 --> 00:13:03.530
What part doesn't fit you anymore?
In the stomach?

00:13:03.530 --> 00:13:05.410
You're suddenly looking for a fight, huh?

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:08.410
Um, in the chest a little bit.

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:10.870
You're kidding!

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:13.790
"Chest growing"!
Where did you hear that urban legend?

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:15.670
Urban legend?

00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:20.630
Right, Eiko. It's an urban legend.
It's impossible!

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:24.180
Eiko, that hurts.

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:26.640
Come on, you're a high school student!

00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:28.970
How could you believe that?

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:33.100
<i>So this is what they call a "mob mentality."</i>

00:13:33.520 --> 00:13:34.310
And so,

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:39.520
I want a new swimsuit, too!

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:42.860
Oh, is your old one suddenly
unable to hold your butt in?

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:43.900
Grrr!

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:45.950
It's not like that at all!

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:47.530
Probably, maybe...

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:51.200
I liked it the last time I wore it.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:58.250
But I went down the water slide
so many times that the material wore out!

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:00.050
You really are a tomboy.

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:02.960
How about you, Hana? About a swimsuit...

00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:06.800
My middle school didn't have a pool,

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:11.560
and I never thought about going
to the beach before.

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:14.430
Let's go! Let's all go together, Hana!

00:14:15.140 --> 00:14:16.560
How about you, Kamu?

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:18.810
I have my school swimsuit.

00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:21.820
The kind that goes down to past the crotch.

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:24.320
The kind that lacks romance?

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:26.570
Don't you wanna just destroy that?

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:27.450
Why?

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:29.990
If you put your finger
under the fabric at the thigh,

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:31.410
don't you think it would feel good?

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:32.660
You have a point!

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:38.210
Since we're on the subject,
let's go to a swimsuit shop together!

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:39.210
Yep.

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:41.840
Then let's go to a nudist beach!

00:14:42.090 --> 00:14:44.090
Then why would we need swimsuits?

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:48.510
What should we do about trying them on?

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:50.760
Of course, you've gotta strip! Buck naked!

00:14:51.010 --> 00:14:51.850
Buck naked?

00:14:52.470 --> 00:14:55.770
Take off your top,
but put it on over your panties.

00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:57.440
I-I see.

00:14:57.690 --> 00:15:01.360
That's why I brought along
an extra pair of my smallest panties.

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:04.280
- I wanna see!
- You're not gonna see.

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:08.240
Shoot. What do they look like?
Are they the kind that's just strings?

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:12.330
Nah, I don't wear stuff like that.

00:15:14.450 --> 00:15:15.330
What do you think?

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:23.000
- Erotic.
- You sure are blunt.

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:25.420
B-But it is daring.

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:26.840
You think?

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:31.590
But I'm most curious
about the panties underneath the suit.

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:33.560
I'm dying of curiosity!

00:15:34.890 --> 00:15:37.100
It's a secret.

00:15:39.310 --> 00:15:42.440
U-Um, what do you think?

00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:44.940
I don't know how to answer that.

00:15:45.730 --> 00:15:47.650
All we can see is your face.

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:49.450
Y-You're right.

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:52.120
Your face is cute.

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:55.990
She hid it.

00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:59.500
Wow, Eiko, you don't
let your guard down, do you?

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:02.500
Excuse me.

00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:04.500
Cute!

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:06.630
That color looks good on you, Hana!

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:09.380
Yeah! It really is cute, Hana!

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:12.050
Yep, I like it.

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:14.720
Thank you.

00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:16.510
But...

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:21.600
I think we look pretty stupid,
peeking in at you like this.

00:16:22.060 --> 00:16:23.190
True.

00:16:23.440 --> 00:16:25.230
S-Sorry.

00:16:26.400 --> 00:16:28.030
Ta-da!

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:31.110
Where did you find that swimsuit?

00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:32.070
A starfish?

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:33.070
A star.

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:34.820
Because it has stars!

00:16:35.660 --> 00:16:37.830
And it's sold normally here!

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:41.410
This must be what they call a "blind spot."

00:16:41.410 --> 00:16:43.880
I must've avoided
looking over there without knowing.

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:44.580
That's mean!

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:47.590
So, what do you think?

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:49.170
It looks good.

00:16:49.170 --> 00:16:50.420
Yeah, it suits you.

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:52.180
I-It does look good.

00:16:52.430 --> 00:16:53.800
- But...
- But?

00:16:54.590 --> 00:16:57.140
Is this a swimsuit
you want to look good in?

00:16:57.470 --> 00:17:00.060
I'm not quite sure
if that's a compliment or not.

00:17:00.310 --> 00:17:01.060
You're mean!

00:17:02.310 --> 00:17:04.810
Kamuri, aren't you going to
try on a swimsuit?

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:06.270
I already bought it.

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:07.860
When?

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:10.570
Shouldn't you try it on first?

00:17:10.820 --> 00:17:15.870
What if you finally put it on and your
body is busting out in all directions?

00:17:15.870 --> 00:17:18.620
What parts of her body
would be busting out in all directions?

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:20.200
I did try it on.

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:22.460
Together with Eiko.

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:26.630
<i>She was there!</i>

00:17:26.630 --> 00:17:28.170
<i>N-Now I remember.</i>

00:17:28.710 --> 00:17:29.750
Kamu, Kamu...

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:33.260
Were Eiko's panties teeny-tiny?

00:17:33.720 --> 00:17:34.510
Ya.

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:36.590
They were stretched really tightly.

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:37.930
Cut it out.

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:43.640
Hana!

00:17:44.770 --> 00:17:46.810
You can swim, can't you?

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:48.820
N-No, I can't!

00:17:49.070 --> 00:17:53.150
I'm bad at all sports,
and there's no exception for swimming!

00:17:53.610 --> 00:17:55.610
I'm not a penguin!

00:17:55.860 --> 00:17:59.280
I am not a penguin! So...

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:01.790
You move like a penguin.

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:03.160
Pen-pen, pen-pen, pen!
Pen-pen, pen-pen, pen!

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:03.160
Cute.

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:08.420
Well, if you drown, we'll be there
to save you, so no worries.

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:10.500
There are three of us, so relax.

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:13.010
That's right!
You're in the hands of experts!

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:15.180
Everyone...

00:18:17.140 --> 00:18:19.350
Well, we've all got our swimsuits!

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:23.480
So on our next day off,
let's go to the beach!

00:18:23.930 --> 00:18:26.350
Good idea. Yeah, let's go.

00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:29.270
Hana, since your apartment
is near the station,

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:32.030
how about we sleep over
the night before?

00:18:33.490 --> 00:18:35.360
That would be
making effective use of time.

00:18:36.150 --> 00:18:37.610
What do you think, Hana?

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:40.490
You're more than welcome!

00:18:40.990 --> 00:18:42.160
I'm looking forward to it!

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:45.580
I can't wait, I can't wait!
Welcome, welcome!

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:43.910
She's acting like a penguin again.

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:45.580
That's cute.

00:18:45.580 --> 00:18:47.000
Pen-pen, pen-pen!

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:16.190
Okay. Once more.

00:19:34.420 --> 00:19:35.760
Good morning, Shion!

00:19:37.220 --> 00:19:39.130
Good morning. You're up early.

00:19:39.840 --> 00:19:41.430
Are you on duty again today?

00:19:41.760 --> 00:19:47.140
No, today I thought I'd help you
get breakfast ready and make lunch.

00:19:49.350 --> 00:19:50.900
Well, I guess I could use a hand.

00:19:51.440 --> 00:19:52.270
Great!

00:19:52.770 --> 00:19:56.280
I apologize for forgetting to bring
the lunch you made the other day.

00:19:57.360 --> 00:19:58.150
That's all right.

00:19:58.860 --> 00:20:01.410
What would be good for your lunch today?

00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:06.790
Huh?

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:10.250
There are three lunchboxes.

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:12.710
For me and Ms. Hannen, too.

00:20:12.960 --> 00:20:14.340
For Hiroe?

00:20:29.020 --> 00:20:30.480
<i>There's Takahashi.</i>

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:42.110
<i>Wh-What should I do?</i>

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:46.530
<i>But I did decide to greet her first today!</i>

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:53.210
Um, Takahashi!

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:56.340
Good morning!

00:20:58.170 --> 00:21:00.340
Good morning, Ichinose.

00:21:01.550 --> 00:21:02.880
<i>I was finally able to say it!</i>

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:07.060
Flowers...

00:21:19.690 --> 00:21:20.490
Are you okay?

00:21:21.110 --> 00:21:22.240
Y-Yeah.

00:21:24.990 --> 00:21:27.660
You've been working hard
on these every morning, huh?

00:21:27.990 --> 00:21:29.490
That's great!

00:21:30.330 --> 00:21:33.080
It's just my turn this week
for Horticulture Club.

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:35.460
But it's still impressive!

00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:38.880
It's tough to grow flowers.

00:21:40.300 --> 00:21:42.050
They're so pretty.

00:21:45.680 --> 00:21:47.930
You know, Ichinose...

00:21:49.140 --> 00:21:54.560
Soon, the mini sunflowers
in this flower bed will bloom.

00:21:55.480 --> 00:21:56.810
Wow!

00:21:57.230 --> 00:22:00.070
I bet this will be
even more beautiful then.

00:22:01.360 --> 00:22:04.950
Listen, when they do bloom,
can I invite you back to see them?

00:22:06.780 --> 00:22:08.950
Sure, Takahashi!
